    "problem": "Water resource assessments in South America are hampered by substantial uncertainties in climate models, where projections range from significant wetting to drying, and over-reliance on the model consensus can be misleading by masking the actual risk of drying in the Amazon basin.",
    "method": "We propose a statistical method using singular value decomposition to identify global-scale climate metrics from present-day observations, which serve to constrain multi-model projections of future runoff changes in the Amazon basin and reduce uncertainty in water resource assessments.",
    "task": "The task is to assess the risk of future drying in the Amazon basin by applying a statistical method that uses observational constraints to reduce uncertainty in runoff projections from multiple climate models.",
